            <div class="item">
                <div class="row">
                    <h3>Annotator-Aware Two-Stage Pipeline for Sexism Detection in Tweets - Master's Applications of Language Processing in Practice Course</h3>
                </div>
                <ul class="details">
                    <li>An empirical study of three system implementations: a fine-tuned Transformer-based system with early and late fusion, a zero-shot autoregressive (AR) LLM-based system, and a zero-shot diffusion LLM-based system.</li>
                    <li>All systems follow the same two-stage pipeline, leverage bilingual fusion by combining original and cross-translated tweets, and integrate annotator demographics.</li>
                    <li>Utilized Python and PyTorch.</li>
                    <li>Published as first author in the CLEF 2025 Working Notes (see Publications).</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
            <div class="item">
                <div class="row">
                    <h3>Dual Dense Upsampling Convolution for Cityscapes Dataset Segmentation - Master's Computer Vision Course</h3>
                </div>
                <ul class="details">
                    <li>Implemented Dual Dense Upsampling Convolution (DDUC) for road scene semantic segmentation using the Cityscapes dataset, based on ICCEA 2024 research.</li>
                    <li>Integrated DDUC into the SegProp framework for semi-supervised segmentation of aerial videos using the RuralScapes dataset.</li>
                    <li>Developed a video inference pipeline to generate segmented video outputs from raw input footage.</li>
                    <li>Built a module to quantify the quality of urban green areas from semantic segmentation results.</li>
                    <li>Utilized Python, PyTorch, OpenCV, and NumPy for model development and evaluation.</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
            <div class="item">
                <div class="row">
                    <h3>Contrail Segmentation - Master's Image Processing Course</h3>
                </div>
                <ul class="details">
                    <li>Conducted contrail segmentation on satellite imagery using deep learning models to support climate change mitigation in aviation.</li>
                    <li>Compared segmentation architectures including UNet, EfficientNetB7+UNet, and CBAM+UNet, using a 450GB dataset from a Kaggle competition.</li>
                    <li>Standardized training with the Adam optimizer, 11 epochs, and consistent hyperparameters across all experiments.</li>
                    <li>Evaluated model performance using the Dice score, testing both BCE and BCE + Dice loss functions.</li>
                    <li>Achieved the highest validation Dice score of 0.555 with EfficientNetB7 + UNet using BCE loss, compared with 0.543 for the baseline UNet.</li>
                    <li>BCE loss alone outperformed BCE + Dice loss across all three architectures, likely due to extreme class sparsity: 70% of validation images contain no contrails, and contrail pixels make up under 1% of the data, which can make the Dice term unstable during training.</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
            <div class="item">
                <div class="row">
                    <h3>CycleGAN-Based Synthetic Image Data Generation for Metallic Surface Defects - Human-Centered Robotics and Automation Laboratory</h3>
                </div>
                <ul class="details">
                    <li>Implemented and adapted CycleGAN to generate synthetic images for a metallic surface defect dataset.</li>
                    <li>The synthetic images were used to add variance to the training data for the metallic surface defect detection model.</li>
                    <li>The model trained on the synthetic data is being tested in a larger Automated Optical Inspection (AOI) system.</li>
                    <li>Published at ICCMA 2025 (see Publications).</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
            <div class="item">
                <div class="row">
                    <h3>Robotic Generative AI 3-Cup and Ball Game - Human-Centered Robotics and Automation Laboratory</h3>
                </div>
                <ul class="details">
                    <li>Developed the vision system of the Robotic Generative AI 3-Cup and Ball Game project.</li>
                    <li>The vision system used YOLOv7 to detect the cups and ball, then the SORT algorithm to track them. This detection and tracking was combined with a custom algorithm to track the ball inside the cup.</li>
                    <li>The project was showcased at Intelligent Asia 2024 in Nangang, Taipei, Taiwan, on August 21-24, 2024, at the National Science and Technology Council booth.</li>
                    <li>Published at CACS 2024 (see Publications).</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
            <div class="item">
                <div class="row">
                    <h3>Video Stabilization with Optical Flow - Bachelor's Image Processing and Computer Vision Course</h3>
                </div>
                <ul class="details">
                    <li>Created a Python program utilizing OpenCV and NumPy.</li>
                    <li>The program used corner detection to find tracking points and optical flow to track them, in order to calculate the displacement caused by shaking.</li>
                    <li>The input is a shaky video, and the output is a stabilized video with the shaking removed.</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
            <div class="item">
                <div class="row">
                    <h3>Ultrasound Image Segmentation and Classification - Bachelor's Image Processing and Computer Vision Course</h3>
                </div>
                <ul class="details">
                    <li>Created a Python script utilizing OpenCV, NumPy, and TensorFlow.</li>
                    <li>The program applied several image processing techniques and a U-Net architecture to segment cancer and tumor areas, then used DenseNet201 to extract features from the segmented regions and classify them as malignant or benign.</li>
                    <li>The metrics used in the project are Receiver Operating Characteristic (ROC), Area Under the Curve (AUC), and Accuracy.</li>
                    <li>The input is ultrasound medical images containing cancer and tumor cases.</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
            <div class="item">
                <div class="row">
                    <h3>Hotel Review Sentiment Analysis - Bachelor's Natural Language Processing Course</h3>
                </div>
                <ul class="details">
                    <li>Created a Python script utilizing Pandas, NumPy, NLTK, and Scikit-Learn.</li>
                    <li>The script implements data selection, six data preprocessing techniques, and classification.</li>
                    <li>The metrics used in the project are Accuracy, Precision, Recall, and F1-score.</li>
                    <li>The input is Tripadvisor hotel review data. The output is a statistical report and analysis.</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </div>

